Segment Insights & Regional Overview
By Type
MRI remains the dominant diagnostic modality due to its superior soft-tissue contrast, high-resolution imaging capabilities, and non-invasive nature. Molecular testing is emerging as a critical tool for personalized care, while PET-CT, EEG, and tissue sampling support accurate tumor characterization and staging.
By Application
Surgery holds the highest market share, serving as the cornerstone of brain tumor management. Advances in neuronavigation, intraoperative MRI, and fluorescence-guided surgery are enhancing resection precision. Complementary modalities such as radiation therapy, chemotherapy, immunotherapy, and targeted therapy continue to expand treatment options.
By End User
Hospitals lead the global market due to their capacity to integrate advanced diagnostics, neurosurgery, radiation therapy, and multi-disciplinary expertise within a single care pathway. Diagnostic centers and cancer research institutes play vital roles in early detection and clinical innovation.
By Therapeutic Approach
Combination therapy is emerging as the leading treatment strategy, aligning surgery with radiation and systemic therapies tailored through molecular profiling. This approach is increasingly recognized as essential for addressing tumor heterogeneity and improving long-term survival.
By Technology Advancement
Imaging technologies dominate the market’s innovation landscape. Functional MRI, PET-MRI hybrids, AI-driven image analytics, and metabolic imaging tools are setting new standards in diagnostic precision and treatment planning.

